[Music]  if there is one thing fans like more  than watching their favorite movies it's  ranking every aspect of them the batman  the latest in a storied history of  batman movies provides fresh fodder for  fans so the real question is pattinson  vs bale who really played the better  batman the dark knight has been played  by so many actors at this point that you  would be hard-pressed to find a person  who doesn't have some sort of ranking  for the collection of actors and their  respective portrayals it used to be that  a favorite batman could be separated by  generation it's now more apt to compare  batman performances based on intention  and tone than anything else especially  when you consider the thematic valleys  between say george clooney and batman  and robin and ben affleck and batman vs  superman dawn of justice some of the  performances however are easy to compare  arguably the two closest being christian  bale and robert pattinson bale portrayed  batman and christopher nolan's famed  dark knight trilogy while robert  pattinson debuted his version of the  caped crusader in this year's the batman  both depictions of batman examine the  early years of the vigilante through a  lens far more grounded in reality than  other more fantastical comic book movies  but which actor do fans think did a  better job bringing a darker dark knight  to life director christopher nolan's  batman begins became one of the most  critically acclaimed comic book films  ever when it was released in 2005  winning near universal praise from both  critics and fans fans have continued to  show support for bale with the actor  even being voted the best batman in a  poll this year from gamespot out of more  than 290 thousand votes bale received 66  percent of the support as the best  batman against competitors ben affleck  adam west and michael keaton while  nolan's the dark knight is the highmark  for many fans regarding batman movies  some are already declaring robert  pattinson and the batman superior even  though the film was only just released  i'm vengeance like bale pattinson has  also won over critics with the batman  currently standing at an 85 percent  fresh rating on rotten tomatoes critic  christie lamyer drew comparisons to  robert de niro and taxi driver in her  review for roger rogerebert.com she said  this is travis bickle in the bath suit  detached and disillusioned he's not just  prepared but hungry to explore this  figure's weird dark instincts there is  plenty to compare when looking at the  performances of christian bale and  robert pattinson in their respective  batman projects both actors turned to  edgy adaptations of the character after  careers building respectable  performances and challenging pieces bale  performed in movies like american psycho  and pattinson more recently with indie  films such as the lighthouse both have  also earned similar praise for their  debut portrayals of batman a character  each shows as a brooding figure as the  beginning of a journey of possible  addiction to his vigilante persona  between the two however bale is the  favorite this may not always be the case  but with three highly praised movies  under his belt bale has earned more  faith with audiences  next to the recent game spot poll  crowning bail as the fans favorite by a  wide margin there is also a 2020 survey  similarly finding bale on the top of the  batman heap while the batman has earned  plenty of praise too bale's movies  remain more universally liked with the  dark knight touching 94 percent with  critics and audiences alike on rotten  tomatoes even the dark knight rises  earned higher marks with critics than  the batman while pattinson is not  dethroned bale it should be noted that  the batman is only his first film and he  hasn't been included in many public  polls if the reviews are any indication  though pattinson could soon be replacing  bale for many as their preferred dark  knight  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the batman are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]

